`--project` pins the query root, and every row carries its whole frontmatter plus a `path`
relative to that root — `plans/alpha/index.md`, not the `elsewhere/`-prefixed path the working
directory would give.

-- fixtures/cwd/elsewhere/plans/alpha/index.md --
---
title: Alpha
status: ready-for-dev
sp: 5
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --project elsewhere --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --output json
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
[
  {
    "title": "Alpha",
    "status": "ready-for-dev",
    "sp": 5,
    "path": "plans/alpha/index.md",
    "slug": "alpha"
  }
]
-- stderr --
